{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning",
    "title": "Treatment Planning",
    "order": 13
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning-abdomen",
    "title": "Abdomen Treatment Planning",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "The Central Challenge \u2014 Motion",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Abdominal organs (liver, pancreas, stomach) move substantially with every breath \u2014 the liver alone can move 1\u20132 cm or more with normal respiration. Managing this motion is the defining planning challenge for this site, more than for almost any other."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Positioning and Motion Management",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Common setup: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "supine, arms up",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (out of the beam path), with a knee/ankle support for comfort and reproducibility. "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "IV contrast",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is frequently used at simulation to help define liver, pancreatic, and vascular anatomy."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "4D-CT",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " captures the tumor's full motion envelope across the breathing cycle, letting you contour an "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "ITV (Internal Target Volume)",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " that accounts for that motion directly. Alternative approaches include "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "breath-hold",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " techniques and "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "respiratory gating",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (treating only during a specific part of the breathing cycle)."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why is 4D-CT particularly important for abdominal treatment planning?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "It captures the target's motion across the breathing cycle, informing the ITV",
              "It provides better bone detail than conventional CT"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "4D-CT's whole purpose here is capturing respiratory-driven target motion so the ITV can be built to actually cover where the tumor moves, not just where it sits on one snapshot."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Target Volumes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Abdominal target volumes follow the standard GTV/CTV/PTV hierarchy, with two site-specific wrinkles:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Volume"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Abdomen-specific consideration"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "GTV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Defined on contrast-enhanced CT (or fused MRI/PET) given how much clearer IV contrast makes liver/pancreatic lesions and adjacent vasculature"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "CTV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "GTV plus a margin for microscopic spread, often edited off natural anatomic barriers (e.g., not extending CTV into bone or outside the peritoneal cavity where disease can't physically spread)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "ITV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "CTV expanded specifically to cover respiratory motion, built directly from the 4D-CT motion envelope covered on the previous page"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "PTV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "ITV plus a smaller setup-margin expansion \u2014 note that in a moving-target site like this, ITV sits "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "between",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "italic"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " CTV and PTV in the expansion sequence, unlike a static site where PTV is simply CTV plus one margin"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In abdominal planning, where does the ITV fit in the volume expansion sequence?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Between CTV and PTV, accounting for motion before the setup margin is added",
              "It replaces the PTV entirely"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "ITV sits between CTV and PTV \u2014 motion is accounted for first (CTV to ITV), then setup uncertainty is added on top (ITV to PTV)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Organ-at-Risk Constraints",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Structure"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Constraint (typical conventional fractionation)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Liver (whole organ)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mean dose \u2264 28\u201330 Gy (uninvolved liver)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Kidneys (bilateral)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mean dose \u2264 18 Gy"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Spinal cord"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "\u2264 45\u201350 Gy"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Small bowel"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "V45 \u2264 195 cc (volume receiving 45 Gy)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Stomach"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "\u2264 45 Gy to a limited volume"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "SBRT for liver lesions uses far tighter, ablative constraints given the much higher dose per fraction \u2014 a genuinely different planning problem than conventional fractionation."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Techniques and Typical Dose",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "IMRT/VMAT",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is standard for conventional abdominal treatment (commonly 45\u201354 Gy in 25\u201330 fractions for pancreatic/gastric disease), allowing dose to be shaped around the many nearby OARs. "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "SBRT",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is increasingly used for small, well-defined liver or pancreatic lesions (commonly 30\u201350 Gy in 3\u20135 fractions) in a limited number of high-dose fractions, but demands excellent motion management (gating or breath-hold) and image guidance given the ablative dose per fraction."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered why motion management dominates abdominal planning, positioning and 4D-CT/ITV concepts, the abdomen-specific target volume sequence, key OAR constraints, and the IMRT/VMAT vs. SBRT technique choice with typical dose ranges."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Cross-reference: for GI sites at the pelvic end of the spectrum (rectal, anal), see the Pelvis lesson instead \u2014 ARRT groups those there, not here."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
